Mix the published token vectors into the Fiat-Shamir transcript.

Part of the SASH eb95bfa build that verifiable-inference-ethereum proves and
verifies with (SPEC.md §1.1). Unlike patches 0001-0005 it changes behaviour, on
both sides: the prover that makes the bundles and the verifier that checks them.
Upstream source is Apache-2.0; this patch modifies it (Apache-2.0 §4(b)).

Upstream never mixes `Fixed.tok_in` or `Fixed.tok_out` into the channel.
`embed_tok_ok` and `head_tok_ok` compare their Horner sums under
`w_residual_stream` with `claims.embed_tok` and `claims.head_tok`, but `w` is
drawn from a transcript the published vectors never entered. Anyone holding a
valid bundle can replay the transcript to `w`, change any token positions and
solve one QM31 equation (four linear equations over M31) for four slack
positions: the claims and every commitment stay as they were and the verifier
accepts the forged vectors.

- prover/src/compose.rs: `pub fn token_transcript_words(tok_in, tok_out)`
  returns `len(tok_in) || tok_in || len(tok_out) || tok_out` as exact `u32`
  words, or `None` when both vectors are empty. `verify_composed` (here
  `verify_composed_parsed`) mixes the words of `fixed.tok_in` and
  `fixed.tok_out` with `mix_u32s` right after committing tree 2 and before
  `Rels::draw`, so every relation element and `w_residual_stream` depend on
  them. The prover computes the two vectors it publishes before its first
  relation draw, mixes the same words at the same position, and publishes the
  same two vectors in `Fixed`.
- prover/src/common.rs: `Op::MixU32s(Vec<u32>)` and `Session::mix_u32s`,
  which mixes and records the words, and the arm that replays them in
  `prove_raw`'s internal verification.

A chunk that publishes neither vector mixes nothing, so its transcript, its
proof and every digest upstream pins for it stay byte-identical. Only a chunk
with the embedding or the argmax proves differently, and only a verifier with
this patch accepts its proof.

